 12 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Horizontal Bar (swinging and slow movements), Parallel Bars, Pommelled Horse, Rings (stationary and swinging movements), and Rope Climb."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The individual championship was known in the " [:strong {} "Official Report"] " as “The Heptathlon” because it encompassed seven events, although they were conducted on only five apparatuses. The winner was the Italian " [:a {:href "/athletes/30470"} "Alberto Braglia"] ", who had been runner-up in both individual events at the " [:a {:href "/editions/4/sports/GAR"} "1906 Olympics in Athens"] ". An article in a Birmingham newspaper noted that Braglia “scored 16 points in the rope climb and 67 of a maximum 72 on the pommel horse.”"] "\n\n" [:p {} "Braglia used his Olympic fame to become a circus performer. Working on a trapeze, he sustained a serious injury from a fall in 1910. However, he recovered from that setback to return in 1912 at Stockholm, where he defended his Olympic title in " [:a {:href "/results/70050"} "individual gymnastics"] ". He then turned professional, returning to the circus as an acrobat. Braglia later returned to gymnastics and coached the Italian team at the " [:a {:href "/editions/10/sports/GAR"} "1932 Olympics"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Full results of this event were not available until March 2020, and were not originally published in the Mallon/Buchanan book " [:strong {} [:em {} "The 1908 Olympic Games: Results for All Competitors in All Events, with Commentary"]] " (McFarland, 2000). Hilary Evans, one of the OlyMADMen, discovered them in an obscure French newspaper/journal, " [:em {} "Les Jeunes: courrier de quinzaine du journal “Le Patronage”"] ", the journal of the Fédération sportive et culturelle de France from 8 August 1908. They can be seen " [:a {:href "https://gallica.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/bpt6k5325208t/f2.item.zoom"} "here"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The late " [:a {:href "/athletes/921847"} "Ian Buchanan"] " once said that “we would find them [1908 individual gymnastics results] somewhere - perhaps in somebody’s attic.” Ian is certainly smiling down upon us, knowing that the full results of the 1908 Olympics are now complete with the addition of these results."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Points"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/30470"} "Alberto Braglia"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ITA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ITA.png"}] "ITA"]] [:td {} "317.00"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/30181"} "Walter Tysall"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} "312.00"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/30028"} "Louis Ségura"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FRA.png"}] "FRA"]] [:td {} "297.00"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/30315"} "Curt Steuernagel"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} "273.50"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "5"] [:td {:class "bib"} "